→ rh1 | 247,500 | 246,666 | $1.40 |\n| 3 | Bridge ETH eth1 → rh1 (gas) | 0.0002 ETH | about 0.0000333 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 4 | rh1: swap WBTC → ETH | 246,666 | about 0.0492 ETH | $0.36 |\n| 5 | Bridge WBTC eth1 → arb1 | 247,500 | 246,666 | $1.40 |\n| 6 | Bridge ETH eth1 → arb1 (gas) | 0.0003 ETH | about 0.000133 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 7 | arb1: swap WBTC → USDC | 246,666 | about 147.70 USDC | $0.36 |\n\n- **Gas legs (3 and 6):** rh1 and arb1 hold 0 ETH, so they can't pay for the swaps in legs 4 and 7. I added small ETH bridges for that.\n  - The ETH bridge fee is a fixed amount, so very small bridges are rejected as too small.\n  - On arb1 I bridged a bit more, so it keeps enough ETH for one more transaction while it holds USDC.\n- **Arbitrum route:** I chose bridging WBTC and swapping on Arbitrum. Swapping on Ethereum and bridging the USDC would cost about $5.30 instead of $3.16, and would pay out less (about 145.0 USDC).\n- **eth1 gas:** eth1 keeps about 0.05 ETH, well above its per-transaction gas reserve.\n\nI'll run the legs one at a time, checking the destination balance after each, once you approve."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":28,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":29,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_13"},"id":"toolu_01TpKa5NkWZ9YBiEDMT44k7T"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":30,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"tx_id\":\"tx_14\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01TpKa5NkWZ9YBiEDMT44k7T","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":31,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_tx_status","arguments":{"tx_id":"tx_14"},"id":"toolu_01PGYkumu5PmWzUQSZRUNsfE"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":32,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"status\":\"confirmed\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01PGYkumu5PmWzUQSZRUNsfE","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_tx_status